{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1102184-10-princes-from-damnation-city","id":1102184,"title":"10 Princes from Damnation City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-09T21:23:25-07:00","id":1102184,"title":"10 Princes from Damnation City","content":"Pretty interesting. Does anyone else have any unique or unusual princes for their cities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T22:37:41-07:00","id":1102198,"title":"","content":"It's funny you mention the 10 Princes. One of the side projects I'm working on is a Requiem Chronicle centered around the Troupe having to deal with a power vacuum and two contenders for Prince vying for loyalty and support. What makes this pertinent to the topic is that the two contenders are based on the Archbishop and Shadow ideas respectively from the 10 Princes section of Damnation City, essentially making it a Archbishop vs. Shadow political Chronicle. Or, more accurately, an evil you know vs. an evil you don't political Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:49:39-07:00","id":1102317,"title":"","content":"I really liked the 10 Princes and used a couple of them played pretty straight in my last vampire game. There were also some other Princes of my own, however.<br /> <br /> It started with Lucian, who was a member of Belial's Brood, specifically the Throne of Smokeless Fire faction, who believe in social dominance in a variety of different ways. His primary tool was money. I used a little from the Reap the Whirlwind story, with him basically having some information on everyone. As the money man, he was available to see for loans, and since a lot of vampires in the domain, Miami, had fled from other domains, they didn't always come with money so he was seen for that. He was fairly lenient with his loans when he needed to be, and would also offer connections to contractors and other people that might allow vampires to get what they need, like a lair or secret hatches in their lairs, special security set up in a ghoul's home, a connection to a business or just a swath of private land where they could raise a cult uninterrupted by modern concerns. Of course, in providing these connections and resources, he was able to find out the more obvious vulnerable areas for most vampires in the city, who they were protecting or where their economic interests were. It didn't help that he had a lot of tendrils in every major piece of infrastructure, from banking to law enforcement, allowing him to keep tabs on things. I suppose in this way as the 'all knowing' he was probably a very traditionally viewed prince, except for his private side. He was the leader of Belial's Brood in the city and assisted the other Brood factions in their attempts to hide and practice.<br /> <br /> His private interests were never disclosed, even after his death. Before he was Prince, he was basically an accountant/adviser for the old Prince, and when the old Prince went into torpor and left him in charge it was accepted that he'd keep things running steady, with people not realizing that he'd already killed the old Prince and was ensuring no one could really stand against him. Vampires who never had their thumb on him thought he was pretty easy going, as he didn't particularly care what you were doing unless you upset the order of things or started getting paranoid about potential Brood activity in the city. Vampires who were under his thumb knew him to be far more harsh and dominating in private but, however much they hated him, could appreciate him for being an appropriately 'alpha' vampire.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately he was done in by a rogue factor. The Tyrant, from Damnation City. An ex-childer of the old Prince who wanted vengeance against him and figured she could make a step in the right direction by eliminating his successor. It threw a lot of the city into turmoil, as at first people thought she had all his records, thus their vulnerabilities, and she was clearly irrational.<br /> <br /> Eventually she was usurped, however. Her own sheriff, Royce, used his position as mediator between her and the various political factions to gain their support for when he overthrew her. In addition, he managed to find Lucian's cache of secret records regarding other vampires, and had a secret of his own. He was an En. An old, old bloodline, no one really knew what that meant except the players, who fled the city after some of their close associates died mysteriously. They had sort of stumbled upon some of his deceits and thought he was covering up his trail and they decided it would be better to skip town for safety. Ironically he wasn't behind the deaths, and was going to reach out to them to be his hounds. Last we saw, he was organizing members of the city to take over surrounding domains, and calling himself King. Very interesting guy, the players really liked him for different reasons and he was, I think, a little eccentric in terms of vampire. Even as sheriff, which is when they started dealing with him, every time he made an appearance he was wearing a different, usually brightly colored, outfit or style.<br /> <br /> I tend to like Princes with secrets, obviously, but they're not always so big. Sometimes it might just be that they're utterly banal in their life beyond the court. But I hadn't played vampire in years and really wanted to get some of my favorite aspects of the game in, like the Brood and diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T13:11:12-07:00","id":1102340,"title":"","content":"Of the two games I've run one had a Gangral from the Circle with a &quot;by this axe I rule&quot; approach and one of my players compleatly missed when she started hitting on him. The other had a demacratic system where each kindred got one clan vote and one open vote with the top two candidates from each clan and the top five remaining from the open vote got to sit on the council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T00:11:06-07:00","id":1108313,"title":"","content":"I decided on having the city being contested by two princes. A Dragon Ordo Dracul Prince who is personally very powerful (lots of coils and other disciplines) who had the Geheim Bloodline with their &quot;Blut Alchemie&quot; (she makes his own money), but with mostly mortal allies. <br /> <br /> Then a Lancea Sanctum Prince who is loosely based on Augusto Vidal, but with Theban Sorcery (original Vidal doesn't have). &quot;Vidal&quot; has more vampire followers, but wasn't directly as powerful and less mortal influence. <br /> <br /> I figured it would be fun to see the players try to play one side off the other, but actually being manipulated instead. Conflict kind of being faith versus science. Also, just the sheer chaos of different Elysiums not being so safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}